  "result": "I found the bug and wrote the fix plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-staged-puppy.md`. Nothing is changed yet, because plan mode allows only read-only work.\n\n**What's wrong:** the options are listed in the right order. The problem is the order of the names inside each entry. An option declared as `-a, --alpha` shows up in `--help` as `--alpha, -a`. A quick test run confirmed this.\n\n**Cause:** in `src/click/formatting.py:319`, `join_options` sorts the names by prefix length with `reverse=True`, which puts the long `--` names first.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n1. Change that line to `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])`. Short names come first again, and names with the same prefix length keep the order they were declared in.\n2. Add a regression test in `tests/test_formatting.py` that checks `--help` shows `-a, --alpha`.\n3. Run the repro again and then the full test suite.\n\nI couldn't open the formal plan-approval step because that tool isn't available in this session. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.",
